===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*meh₂d-|id=wet}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mete}}, from {{inh|en|ang|mete||food}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*mati}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*matiz|t=food}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*meh₂d-|id=wet|t=to drip, ooze; grease, fat}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|mete}}, {{cog|osx|meti}}, {{cog|goh|maz||food}}, {{cog|is|matur}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐍄𐍃}}.

A ''-ja-'' derivation from the same base is found in {{cog|dum|-}} and {{cog|gml|met||lean pork}}, from which {{cog|nl|met||minced pork}} and {{cog|de|Mett||minced meat}} derive, respectively. Compare also {{cog|sga|mess|t=animal feed}} and {{cog|cy|mes|t=acorns}}, {{cog|en|mast|t=fodder for swine and other animals}}, which are probably from the same root.

